==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|каранда́шъ||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
In Russian from the 16–17th centuries. Borrowing from a {{der|ru|trk}} language. Compare {{cog|tr|karataş||black slate}}, composed of {{m|tr|kara||black}} + {{m|tr|taş||stone}}, {{cog|tt|кара таш||graphite, black lead}}. The origin of epenthetic {{m|ru||-н-}} is unclear. Compare {{m|ru|каланча́}} for the same epenthesis.

